,"kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CoreNumbers","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The core decomposition of an undirected graph (Batagelj–Zaversnik), over its simple graph. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s core number is the largest k such that it lies in a subgraph where every vertex has at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least k neighbors."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/TrussNumbers":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/trussnumbers","title":"TrussNumbers","abstract":[{"text":"The truss decomposition of an undirected graph (Cohen; Wang–Cheng), over its simple graph. An","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge’s truss number is the largest k such that it lies in a subgraph where every edge is in at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"least k − 2 triangles: 2 for an edge in no triangle, k for an edge of a k-clique. Parallel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edges share their simple edge’s number, and a self-loop has none.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/TrussNumbers","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrussNumbers"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TrussNumbers"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degeneracy d.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","title":"MaximalCliques","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/AllCliques":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/AllCliques","title":"AllCliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/allcliques","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AllCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AllCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph whose size is in a range, once each, lazily,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order (by vertex index). The order is by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then depth first, each clique followed by its extensions by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"later vertices in ascending index. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating again gives the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d) bitset words per clique for degeneracy d.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques","title":"Cliques","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/OnionLayers":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/OnionLayers","title":"OnionLayers","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/onionlayers","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OnionLayers","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"OnionLayers","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The onion decomposition of an undirected graph’s simple graph: each vertex’s layer, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refinement of the core decomposition in which every layer lies inside one k-shell. Layers are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"numbered from 1; isolated vertices, when there are any, are layer 1 alone.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/TreeDecomposition":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/treedecomposition","title":"TreeDecomposition","abstract":[{"text":"A tree decomposition of a graph: bags of vertices, joined by edges into a tree, such that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every vertex is in a bag, both ends of every edge are together in a bag, and the bags holding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any one vertex form a connected subtree.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/TreeDecomposition","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TreeDecomposition","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TreeDecomposition","kind":"identifier"}]}}}